--- now ---
'the moment now' is a number of seconds since 1970, and the year it names has reached 2026: 1
--- civil time to a moment ---
'the moment of' 2026-07-29 is the number 1785283200
'the moment at' 2026-07-29 16:02:48 is 1785340968
day 32 of january normalises to 1 february: 1
--- a moment to its parts ---
year 2026, month 7, day 29
hour 16, minute 2, second 48
weekday 3 (1 Monday .. 7 Sunday), day of year 210
iso week 31 of iso year 2026
quarter 3, century 20
--- names ---
month 7 is July, or Jul for short
weekday 3 is Wednesday, or Wed for short
a month outside 1..12 has no name: []
--- calendar facts ---
2024 is a leap year: 1, and 2023 is: 0
february 2024 has 29 days; february 2023 has 28
29 february 2024 is a valid date: 1, 29 february 2023 is: 0
24:00:00 is a valid time: 0
--- moving around the calendar ---
a week later: 2026-08-05
31 january plus one month clamps to: 2026-02-28
start of the day: 2026-07-29 00:00:00
start of the week (monday on or before): 2026-07-27
the next monday on or after: 2026-08-03
days between new year and this moment: 209
--- writing a moment out ---
any layout: Wednesday, 29 July 2026 at 16:02
'the date of': 2026-07-29
'the date and time of': 2026-07-29T16:02:48+00:00
'the rfc 3339 date and time of': 2026-07-29 16:02:48+00:00
'the rfc email date of': Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:02:48 +0000
'the moment in words of': Wed Jul 29 16:02:48 UTC 2026
--- reading a moment in ---
'2026-07-29' reads as 2026-07-29
'20260729T160248' reads as 2026-07-29 16:02:48
'29 July 2026' reads as 2026-07-29
'2026-02-30' does not exist, and reads as a moment: 0
garbage reads as a moment: 0, and reading it anyway gives: 0
--- relative descriptions ---
the base moment is Sunday 2026-09-27
'3 weeks ago' from there is 2026-09-06
'next wednesday' from there is 2026-09-30
'2026-01-01 + 7 days' is 2026-01-08, ignoring the base entirely since it names its own absolute moment
'next wednesday' reads as a description: 1
garbage reads as a description: 0
